   149	## Acceptance
   150	
   151	- Give the model every whole item with its category prompt; record the settings version.
   152	- Every evidence link targets a shown thesis or current candidate. Reject missing or invalid targets with reasons.
   153	- Repeated statements of the same fact within one item, including text/table repetitions, produce one evidence item with multiple references.
   154	- Evidence contains a quotation, standalone summary, speaker, original source, tier and event time. A candidate contains subject, asset/theme kind, focus, question, ladder, due date, association and at least one evidence item; personal-memo candidates may lack evidence. Themes select from block 3 or clearly identify a new issue; assets use a symbol or registered name.
   155	- Every thesis and evidence item has a source. Reject absent quotes/cells or numbers not printed in the cited location, recording the reason.
   156	- Extraction does not mutate the library. Return evidence, candidates and associations together without a separate clustering call. Reference and semantic criteria are owned by the [grouping contract](06-views.md#research-groups-associate-during-extraction); similar names or equal counts do not prove correct grouping.
   157	- Retry from the failed step and replace only that attempt's own result.
   158	
