   184	## Determine associations during extraction
   185	
   186	<!-- generated: relations -->
   187	- D149 requirement: while reading the full text, decide which continuing business process each candidate belongs to, called a research group. Rubin shipments and SK factory deployment retain separate questions while sharing the Rubin rollout group. Group during extraction, not in the frontend or a later whole-library clustering pass.
   188	- Return evidence and candidates separately. Each candidate also carries structured associations; new groups have a name and scope. Mentioning a relationship only in prose is not a complete handoff. Extraction is read-only; the library's “Research groups: associate during extraction” section owns the full handoff and storage contract.
   189	- Grouping remains a target requirement, not a default-pipeline handoff. D155 fixed reference-list vetoes, period/scope rewriting and same-batch duplicates; that does not prove grouping works. See docs/poc/grouping-improvement-plan.md for steps and measurements.
