   202	
   203	<!-- generated: intake-example -->
   204	```
   205	Three items, starting with an empty library (Illustration)
   206	├─ NVIDIA 8-K, April 15, 2025 → Empty library; two candidates arrive | Empty comparison lists; open both as new theses
   207	│   ├─ #1 Theme thesis → China export licensing for this chip class: event (Evidence: H20 exports to China require a licence (fact))
   208	│   └─ #2 NVDA asset thesis → FY2026 China revenue: numeric (Evidence: expected charges up to approximately $5.5 billion (party statement); depends on #1, with easing bullish)
   209	├─ AMD 8-K, April 16, 2025 → AMD has no existing theses; two candidates arrive | Match
   210	│   ├─ Candidate: MI308 export licensing to China → Merge into #1 (Search finds #1. The model identifies the same question: the same chip class under the same rule. AMD's MI308 statement is new evidence. #1 is rejudged but declares its conclusion unchanged: an additional affected model does not change the key facts or rung. #2 is therefore not rejudged.)
   211	│   └─ Candidate: AMD 2025 China revenue → New thesis #3 (AMD has no open thesis; evidence is expected charges up to approximately $800 million (party statement))
   212	└─ Reuters, April 16, 2025, retelling NVIDIA's 8-K → Existing context: #2 and its dependency #1 | Match
   213	    └─ Evidence links to #1 and #2 → Both are repeats (The original source is the same NVIDIA 8-K and both statements already exist under #1 and #2. Add a source reference to each; neither thesis is rejudged.)
   214	```
