   352	## Open questions
   353	
   354	<!-- generated: open -->
   355	- Search method and ranking remain open: semantic, keyword or both. Test on stored information during implementation. Start with top 10 and adjust during experiments.
   356	- Thesis granularity needs a separate decision. Current rules merge a part into its existing thesis and reject overly broad questions. A material segment deserves its own question: NVDA China revenue must not disappear into total revenue. Overly broad units reduce all theses to financial metrics, which is wrong. Research what hedge-fund theses look like, what to merge/split and how many questions to track per subject; the discussion assumes analysts focus on 2–3 per company.
   357	- Labelling details remain open: who, how many, which interface, model evaluation and training, handover to a smaller model, and checks for omitted or mislinked extraction evidence.
