   325	## Module contracts
   326	
   327	| Module | Exchange |
   328	|---|---|
   329	| Extraction | Receive sourced evidence, candidates, associations and necessary group definitions. Supply open subject theses and their dependencies: question, focus, due date and links, without states/evidence, plus available groups under this contract. |
   330	| Config | Read matching/rejudgement settings and search count; record the version with every call. |
   331	| Pull mode | Receive day-end/scheduled updates and due-date freezing/closure; remaining design is deferred. |
   332	| Final verdict | Whether it remains separate is deferred; due-date freezing is decided. |
   333	| Human review pool | Send proposed out-of-universe themes and repeated failures. Resolvable out-of-universe assets receive only processing-log entries. |
   334	| Matching labels | Supply every comparison record; receive human labels and, later, a smaller model. |
   335	
   336	## Acceptance
   337	
   338	- Preserve extraction's associations against final thesis IDs and trace real evidence links under the [grouping contract](#research-groups-associate-during-extraction). Default integration is pending; isolated code checks do not satisfy this acceptance.
   339	- Every thesis has an immutable question, ladder and due date; five rungs or two for yes/no, with exhaustive, non-overlapping, verifiable outcomes.
   340	- Numeric theses name the year and open at most one per subject/quantity for this year and next year; a previous year can remain open until due. Events have one open thesis per event. These are matching-time rules, excluding manual reopening.
   341	- Candidate search covers all open and closed theses, taking top N before comparison. Evidence search stays within its thesis.
   342	- Every comparison records shown input, raw response, Config version and decision maker. Reject destinations outside the shown lists or relevant evidence, and dependencies not shown or explicitly awaiting a chain/year, including cycles.
   343	- Classify every evidence comparison as repeat, replace or new. A repeat adds a reference without rejudging existing links; a new link to an open thesis triggers its rejudgement. Replaced evidence stays in history.
   344	- Store evidence once across multiple thesis links. Carry other links to replacement evidence.
   345	- Rejudge only open theses with changed inputs: new, replaced or newly linked evidence, or changed dependency conclusions. Memo-derived theses without evidence remain unjudged. Cite evidence and relevant dependency IDs, and declare conclusion change. First judgement and rung changes must declare a change. Only facts can establish which rung holds.
   346	- Choose dependencies during matching from shown theses or explicitly awaited chain/years. Numeric dependencies read the specified year; event dependencies follow succession. No cycles.
   347	- Judge dependencies before dependants and each thesis once per item round.
   348	- Append records without rewriting them. Trace all theses, evidence, links and matching records to their origins, and source items to created theses and sourced evidence.
   349	- Append knowledge in arrival order. Log obsolete late statements without adding them; accept newly learned matters with their true dates. A revised retelling changes only its own source reference. Original-source revisions replace changed statements and mark deleted ones replaced.
   350	- Retain every comparison; send code-refused and random samples for human labelling.
   351	
   352	## Open questions
   353	
   354	<!-- generated: open -->
   355	- Search method and ranking remain open: semantic, keyword or both. Test on stored information during implementation. Start with top 10 and adjust during experiments.
   356	- Thesis granularity needs a separate decision. Current rules merge a part into its existing thesis and reject overly broad questions. A material segment deserves its own question: NVDA China revenue must not disappear into total revenue. Overly broad units reduce all theses to financial metrics, which is wrong. Research what hedge-fund theses look like, what to merge/split and how many questions to track per subject; the discussion assumes analysts focus on 2–3 per company.
   357	- Labelling details remain open: who, how many, which interface, model evaluation and training, handover to a smaller model, and checks for omitted or mislinked extraction evidence.
   358	- Design pull mode later: day-end/scheduled execution, overall review, and whether final verdict remains a separate step.
